<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yamparika</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Yamparika Comanche</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Yamparika, or Yap Eaters, named after a root they gathered, were the northernmost division of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comanche">Comanche</a>. They ranged along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arkansas">Arkansas</a> River in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colorado">Colorado</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kansas">Kansas</a> and traded and fought with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cheyenne">Cheyenne</a>, Arapaho and Kiowa. They signed the Medicine Lodge Treaty of 1867 and were settled on the Kiowa-Comanche reservation in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-territory">Indian Territory</a>.</p></div>
